● That's the right instinct, and it's exactly what chafa does internally: pick
  the best glyph per cell from a symbol set by minimising error against the
  source. The map already has this idea — canvas.rs has braille and quadrant
  families competing for a cell.

  Braille buys 2×4 sub-cell precision but is dotted, so it can't fill; blocks
  fill solidly but are coarse. Searching both (plus quadrants and eighth-blocks)
  picks whichever actually wins per cell.

