  netjail is now two halves answering two different questions — what can this 
  process reach, and what did it try to reach.

  Isolation is drawn as a stack because that's what it is: L1 and L2 inside the
  namespace, L3–L5 on the host, with the highlight walking so all five get read
  rather than one being the permanent subject. Observability is the half a
  sandbox usually gets wrong — a log that records enough to be useful usually
  records enough to be a leak. So it shows events arriving over a unix socket
  (not a tail, so rotation can't make it miss anything), and two columns:
  recorded against cannot exist. Not "filtered" — internal/events imports
  nothing from net/http, so no type in it can hold a header. And
  $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR unset means refuse to start.

