  together: web against Flutter desktop on macOS/Windows/Linux, which is why the
  decision core exists twice and why conformance vectors have to hold the
  copies equal. The segment buffer with the playhead inside it, and a seek
  that's free or costs a fetch depending on where it lands — the cache is part
  of the sync mechanism, not an implementation detail. And LiveKit as a boxed
  second real-time system with its own waveform, "its own clock, its own jitter
  buffer, running beside the loop, not inside it."

